WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:06.839
Okay, let's have another crack at how big

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.360
Graham's number is.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.240
Let's start with

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.929
3 arrow 3, this is just 3 to

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:18.240
the power of 3, bang bang bang. That's

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.640
27. The arrow meant this number to this

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.119
power, simple enough. Now

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:30.750
how about 3 double arrow 3? When

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.910
we have a double arrow we're essentially

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.899
saying take this leading number and

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:38.700
string it out with single arrows like

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.600
this and do it this number of times. So

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.610
if the second number had been, say, 10

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.510
we'd have had 10 3s like this.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.100
Luckily the second number was just a

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.190
3 so we have a manageable three

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:57.780
3s; 3 arrow 3 arrow 3. Now

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.719
we know what a single arrow means, so 3

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:04.400
to the power of 3 arrow 3.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.890
Now we know from a moment ago that 3

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.640
arrow 3 was 27, so we have 3 to

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.450
the 27; bang bang, bang, 
bang, bang, that's

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:18.410
about 7.6 trillion. Another

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.270
way to think about double arrows, which

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.250
is very helpful, is that you are building

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.400
a tower of this number of this height. So

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.070
in our example, a tower of 3s which

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.760
is 3 high. And here when you work it

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.890
out you go from top to bottom and right

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.720
to left. A 27 here, 7.6 trillion

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.410
overall. So there's 3 double arrow

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.360
3, a pretty big number;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.010
what about 3 triple arrow 3? Well

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.260
just like double arrows created a string

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.650
of single arrows, triple arrows create a

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.740
string of double arrows. Take the lead

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.590
number, again 3 in our example, and

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.560
string it out like this: 3 double

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.940
arrow 3 double arrow 3 
double arrow; etc etc.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.320
Again, if the trailing number had been

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.100
say 10 it would have looked like this

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:20.000
with ten 3s, but again luckily the

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.770
trailing number here was a measly 3

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.040
so we only need three 3s. This is

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.470
what we're left with: 3 double arrow

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.980
3 double arrow 3. Now remember

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.720
what I said about double arrows

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.020
representing that power tower? So now

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.780
we're saying we're towering this number,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.610
3, and the tower is this number high,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:46.130
3 double arrow 3. Now we already

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.680
saw that 3 double arrow 3 is

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.890
actually about 7.6 trillion;

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.519
so that's our tower height. Imagine that,

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:58.643
a tower of 3s that is

00:02:58.643 --> 00:03:02.840
7.6 trillion digits high. Starting at the

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.840
very top, working right to left, here we

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.360
are at the summit; we have 3 to the

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:13.229
3, that's 27, then down a step

00:03:13.229 --> 00:03:16.340
7.6 trillion now. And now we work

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.670
all the way down this epic tower,

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:22.340
trillions of times; the number getting

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.239
crazily big with each step down. By the

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.400
time we get down to base camp here at

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.320
the very bottom we will have created a

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.630
number so big it doesn't even bear

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.850
thinking about.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:37.220
Isn't this arrow notation amazing? Just

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.389
adding single arrows between the 3s took

00:03:41.389 --> 00:03:44.950
us from 27 to 7.6 trillion

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.930
to a number that seems beyond

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.370
comprehension. Now you can probably guess

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:56.359
what a monster 3 four arrow 3 is going to

00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:00.380
be. This expands to 3 triple arrow 3

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.540
triple arrow 3. Now triple arrows mean

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:07.730
3 double arrow followed by this

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.910
chain.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:12.030
But now the trailing number that tells

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.340
us what to put here and how long the

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.880
chain is going to be happens to be 3

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.790
triple arrow 3; and we know that

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.380
number is ridiculous

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.840
so this chain is going to be pretty darn

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.840
long. And knowing what these double

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.580
arrows mean, we have to start

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.980
constructing another of these enormous

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.670
power towers, but this time the height of

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.970
our tower is going to be figured out

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.850
using this beast of a number. So let's

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.220
see how this plays out; we start here

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.130
with 3 to the 27, already a

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.590
pretty big number, but that just tells us

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.930
the height of the tower below, how many

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.180
3s that are here. But this number

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.910
just tells us the height of another

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.640
tower of 3s below that. And this

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.830
continues, each whopper of a number

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.320
simply telling us how many 3s there

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.630
are in the tower below it; you keep

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.510
building down. And how many layers do you

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:13.860
build down? Well this number, 3 three

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.640
arrow 3 which is unimaginable in itself;

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.150
so can you imagine how big the final

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.970
tower of 3s must be after we've

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.770
iterated all the way through this

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:29.160
process? Can you imagine that? I think

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.950
you're probably can't.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:38.410
Let's call this monstrosity G1. Is that

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:41.680
Graham's number? Nowhere near it.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.950
What we do is we now take another pair

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:47.340
of 3s and the number of arrows

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:53.080
between them is 3 four arrow 3 -G1. That's

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.450
not the number of digits here, that's not

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.250
even the number of powers we're talking

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.340
about - that is the number of arrows; and

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.250
we've shown how quickly arrows can blow

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.600
things up beyond belief. Now we can't

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.701
even count the arrows!
- Boy, that escalated quickly.

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:15.720
Let's call this new number G2.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.630
Now take another pair of 3s; how many

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.460
arrows are we going to put between these

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:27.180
ones? You guessed it - G2. 
This gives us G3.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.920
Then we do it again and we keep

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.980
repeating the process; the huge number we

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.220
get becomes the number of arrows in the

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:39.030
next number. And you keep doing this

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:42.900
64 times. When you finally finish,

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.560
there you go,

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:48.010
you have Graham's number.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.490
This is the upper bound to an answer to

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.830
a reasonably simple question involving

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.920
coloured lines between vertices on cubes

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:00.130
in higher dimensions. That's explained in

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:02.110
another video by Ron Graham himself.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:04.120
Check out the links that are on the

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.770
screen or in the video description.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.910
But this is such a big number, that 2 to

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:13.500
that power and that power are kind of

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.850
hard to distinguish, it's such a big

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:18.030
number.

